# Normalize all text files to LF in the repository, regardless of a contributor's
# local core.autocrlf setting. Without this, a Windows checkout (core.autocrlf=true)
# reads working-tree files back with CRLF when a build script computes a byte-size or
# sha256 for a manifest (e.g. data/distribution/manifest.json), producing values that
# diverge from a Linux CI checkout of the same LF-stored git blob -- surfacing as a
# large, spurious "committed build outputs diverge" failure unrelated to any real
# content change. See PR #228 for a concrete instance of this failure and its fix.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Genuine binary formats: never treat as text, never touch line endings.
*.shp binary
*.shx binary
*.dbf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
